#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489330} :activity/id #uuid "a5e50e5c-f6d4-570d-8bfd-dd50d0a5e6dd" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049970 :topic/id #uuid "22979210-8cd9-5db4-861d-faf167d0a850" :topic/math-academy-id 2124} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489319 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489280 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d911574-ccd3-5c98-bd89-40abf5381b05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488566} {:answer/id #uuid "2e54bdc8-061f-5aca-ad4c-768aadfc8c96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488570} {:answer/id #uuid "96ca6b9c-ffc7-5276-bee4-ff0be2c4198c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488774} {:answer/id #uuid "e1378868-2a9d-52dd-8e6a-ac7feee66d57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488938} {:answer/id #uuid "f00d63d7-b728-5541-b6c4-ed9e9411144d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488977}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488570} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0ad7dc8-4543-5cca-8939-06979b0f56c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e47080dd-98d4-5498-967c-b6d64e7e3867" :question/math-academy-id "q-40629" :question/problem "Verify whether the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent, and find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we verify whether ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}↔{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, the pivot columns correspond to the linearly independent vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ that form the basis of our span.\n\nNow, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the linearly independent columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "55b0eb69-ee74-5a65-98a4-635c7ba90856" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489378}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489330 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23c5f794-99b0-5846-9311-18d5de992953" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488543} {:answer/id #uuid "8d1837d2-279c-5b39-b335-7e4e449a5f14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488750} {:answer/id #uuid "908d17a2-f2f1-56f9-acd8-74a95eb4695f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488758} {:answer/id #uuid "a33bde79-ffb2-5dbe-bf12-ffd8a5fc10a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488794} {:answer/id #uuid "db1a839b-51b6-5277-a632-d4ded0706f14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488925}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488794} :answer-field/id #uuid "878a4e45-5d30-5f1c-aefb-67035a88d122" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c6ef098f-928d-59a3-9d4f-bfcb112bab97" :question/math-academy-id "q-39869" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{v,w\\}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 19\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 28\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}19 & -7 \\\\ -7 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 28\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "772f1302-aeb0-5063-a912-a0f326d01ac2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489353}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489337 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388967 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1b1ee61-1308-5d61-b7ed-da45b7cfca5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388969} {:answer/id #uuid "f88bb249-b083-5351-9669-33db5c6b2547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388970} {:answer/id #uuid "d77cc695-36e6-5192-b27f-3e733685eb86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388971} {:answer/id #uuid "55a3f1da-3779-59ce-ae0d-0dbecdb726b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388972} {:answer/id #uuid "053ae894-bb63-5ac6-b828-d9ea6bb6af7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388973}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388972} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa6cde22-2f73-519a-945c-bffdd259e21b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388968}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dd7403df-a496-59c6-8226-c07a3e6dd8d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-158123" :question/problem "Find the vector in the subspace spanned by $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ \nthat is closest to the vector $x,$ where \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe closest vector to $x$ in the subspace spanned by $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace, which is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8bf7a2d1-6483-574a-bd3f-c2612cb3dafd"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489353 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f402a3a-4f08-5c72-a337-37b1173065e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488572} {:answer/id #uuid "69d00f66-bac7-5a07-842c-86c8ae454700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488678} {:answer/id #uuid "795fe3b9-08f5-5072-9238-46b50ec1f87a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488709} {:answer/id #uuid "924789e2-65b9-582c-b2a0-b829c5928e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488762} {:answer/id #uuid "94182863-ea1a-5c03-b764-976abf2d1657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488768}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488678} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ae069ad-82b0-5089-9f78-df2bcd3c3331" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489064}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "86358ef9-78e9-5caa-a7a3-a7c614e96d69" :question/math-academy-id "q-40628" :question/problem "Verify whether the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent, and find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we verify whether ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, the pivot columns correspond to the linearly independent vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ that form the basis of our span.\n\nNow, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the linearly independent columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ad4ab2c8-0a51-5f88-9dd3-02a2bc3345a4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489319}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489378 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394738 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de82d8c-ce23-555b-bc98-20cd4b7e3d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394740} {:answer/id #uuid "9d838a17-fcf6-5cd8-b98f-01a452dd4e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394741} {:answer/id #uuid "931f8ee6-6ee9-5feb-989f-f94e1f389d53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394742} {:answer/id #uuid "134407e9-0936-586f-9d57-4a275793781d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394743} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb70189-b1c1-5b51-aee9-863f62dd9e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394744}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394744} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2d2041b-3a0c-511a-ae57-4e83abdb08e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "734db729-9741-5fdd-a351-d012beb5fb6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-86761" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{v,w\\}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}11 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{74}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "eff9b1cb-cb04-5ebf-80e3-b9dafaf06cbe" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489337}}] :activity/title "Projecting Vectors Onto Subspaces in Euclidean Spaces (Arbitrary Bases)" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488461}]}
